    "description": "An Iranian urban master plan, or tarh-e jame, establishes a long-term framework for a city's land uses, major connections, public facilities, and related regulations. Its broad proposals must be distinguished from detailed planning and from evidence that development has actually occurred.",
    "tags": ["Master plans", "Comprehensive planning", "Land use", "Tehran", "Urban history"],
    "status": null,
    "editorial_status": "needs_research",
    "as_of_date": "2026-10-26",
